Article 1 An actor who falls under any of the following circumstances may be deemed to have manipulated securities or futures markets by "other methods" as provided in Item (4) of Paragraph 1 of Article 182 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) Using false or uncertain material information to induce investors to make investment decisions, affecting the trading price or volume of securities or futures, and conducting related transactions or seeking related benefits;
(2) By publicly making evaluations, forecasts or investment recommendations on securities and their issuers, listed companies, or futures trading targets, misleading investors to make investment decisions, affecting the trading price or volume of securities or futures, and conducting securities transactions or related futures transactions contrary to the direction of such evaluations, forecasts or investment recommendations;
(3) By planning or implementing false material matters such as asset acquisition or restructuring, investment in new businesses, equity transfer, or acquisition of listed companies, misleading investors to make investment decisions, affecting the trading price or volume of securities, and conducting related transactions or seeking related benefits;
(4) By controlling the generation of information of the issuer or listed company or controlling the content, timing or pace of information disclosure, misleading investors to make investment decisions, affecting the trading price or volume of securities, and conducting related transactions or seeking related benefits;
(5) Without the purpose of concluding transactions, frequently placing or canceling orders, or placing or canceling large orders, misleading investors to make investment decisions, affecting the trading price or volume of securities or futures, and conducting transactions contrary to the orders or seeking related benefits;
(6) By hoarding physical goods, affecting the market conditions of specific futures products, and conducting related futures transactions;
(7) Manipulating securities or futures markets by other methods.

Article 2 Manipulating securities or futures markets, under any of the following circumstances, shall be deemed as "serious circumstances" as provided in Paragraph 1 of Article 182 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) Holding or actually controlling the number of outstanding shares of a security reaching more than 10% of the total number of actual outstanding shares of that security, and committing the act of manipulating the securities market under Item (1) of Paragraph 1 of Article 182, with the cumulative trading volume over ten consecutive trading days reaching more than 20% of the total trading volume of that security during the same period;
(2) Committing the act of manipulating the securities market under Items (2) or (3) of Paragraph 1 of Article 182, with the cumulative trading volume over ten consecutive trading days reaching more than 20% of the total trading volume of that security during the same period;
(3) Committing the act of manipulating the securities market under Items (1) to (4) of Article 1 of this Interpretation, with the total transaction amount of securities trading reaching more than RMB 10 million;
(4) Committing the act of manipulating the futures market under Item (1) of Paragraph 1 of Article 182 and Item (6) of Article 1 of this Interpretation, with the highest combined position of the actually controlled accounts over ten consecutive trading days exceeding twice the position limit standard of the futures exchange, the cumulative trading volume reaching more than 20% of the total trading volume of the relevant futures contract during the same period, and the margin amount occupied for futures trading being more than RMB 5 million;
(5) Committing the act of manipulating the futures market under Items (2) or (3) of Paragraph 1 of Article 182 and Items (1) or (2) of Article 1 of this Interpretation, with the cumulative trading volume of the actually controlled accounts over ten consecutive trading days reaching more than 20% of the total trading volume of the relevant futures contract during the same period, and the margin amount occupied for futures trading being more than RMB 5 million;
(6) Committing the act of manipulating securities or futures markets under Item (5) of Article 1 of this Interpretation, with the cumulative amount of withdrawn orders on that day reaching more than 50% of the total order amount of the relevant security or futures contract during the same period, and the amount of withdrawn securities orders being more than RMB 10 million, or the margin amount occupied for the withdrawn futures contract orders being more than RMB 5 million;
(7) Committing an act of manipulating securities or futures markets, with the amount of illegal gains reaching more than RMB 1 million.

Article 3 Manipulating securities or futures markets, where the amount of illegal gains is more than RMB 500,000, and under any of the following circumstances, shall be deemed as "serious circumstances" as provided in Paragraph 1 of Article 182 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) The issuer, listed company, and its directors, supervisors, senior officers, controlling shareholders or actual controllers commit the act of manipulating securities or futures markets;
(2) The acquirer, the counterparty to a material asset restructuring, and its directors, supervisors, senior officers, controlling shareholders or actual controllers commit the act of manipulating securities or futures markets;
(3) The actor, knowing that the act of manipulating securities or futures markets is under investigation by relevant authorities, continues to commit the act;
(4) Having been subject to criminal liability for manipulating securities or futures markets;
(5) Having been subject to administrative penalties for manipulating securities or futures markets within the past two years;
(6) Manipulating securities or futures markets during special periods such as when the market experiences significant abnormal fluctuations;
(7) Causing adverse social impact or other serious consequences.

Article 4 Under any of the following circumstances, it shall be deemed as "particularly serious circumstances" as provided in Paragraph 1 of Article 182 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) Holding or actually controlling the number of outstanding shares of a security reaching more than 10% of the total number of actual outstanding shares of that security, and committing the act of manipulating the securities market under Item (1) of Paragraph 1 of Article 182, with the cumulative trading volume over ten consecutive trading days reaching more than 50% of the total trading volume of that security during the same period;
(2) Committing the act of manipulating the securities market under Items (2) or (3) of Paragraph 1 of Article 182, with the cumulative trading volume over ten consecutive trading days reaching more than 50% of the total trading volume of that security during the same period;
(3) Committing the act of manipulating the securities market under Items (1) to (4) of Article 1 of this Interpretation, with the total transaction amount of securities trading reaching more than RMB 50 million;
(4) Committing the act of manipulating the futures market under Item (1) of Paragraph 1 of Article 182 and Item (6) of Article 1 of this Interpretation, with the highest combined position of the actually controlled accounts over ten consecutive trading days exceeding five times the position limit standard of the futures exchange, the cumulative trading volume reaching more than 50% of the total trading volume of the relevant futures contract during the same period, and the margin amount occupied for futures trading being more than RMB 25 million;
(5) Committing the act of manipulating the futures market under Items (2) or (3) of Paragraph 1 of Article 182 and Items (1) or (2) of Article 1 of this Interpretation, with the cumulative trading volume of the actually controlled accounts over ten consecutive trading days reaching more than 50% of the total trading volume of the relevant futures contract during the same period, and the margin amount occupied for futures trading being more than RMB 25 million;
(6) Committing an act of manipulating securities or futures markets, with the amount of illegal gains reaching more than RMB 10 million.
If an act of manipulating securities or futures markets is committed, the amount of illegal gains is more than RMB 5 million, and one of the seven circumstances provided in Article 3 of this Interpretation is present, it shall be deemed as "particularly serious circumstances".

Article 5 The following accounts shall be deemed as "accounts actually controlled by oneself" as provided in Article 182 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) Real-name accounts opened and used by the actor in his or her own name;
(2) Accounts of another person into or from which the actor transfers funds and bears actual profits or losses;
(3) Accounts of another person managed, controlled or used by the actor in ways other than those provided in Items (1) and (2);
(4) Accounts of another person over whose assets the actor exercises transaction decision-making rights through investment relationships, agreements, or other means;
(5) Other accounts for which there is evidence proving that the actor has transaction decision-making rights.
Except where there is evidence proving that the actor does not have transaction decision-making rights over the assets in the accounts referred to in Items (1) to (3) of the preceding paragraph.
